  "definitions": {
    "constructed_native_neighborhood": "Each canonical anchor is a literal vertex of a designated deck/runner box. Primary part is chosen by constructive sign role. Before positive scaling, step=min(0.030 m,0.7*minimum primary-part side). Thirty-seven registered points are endpoint index0, three samples at .2/.5/.8 of each of3 edges (1..9), and3x3 interior grid points at .2/.5/.8 on each of3 incident face patches (10..36). V129 scales mesh, anchors, quads and witnesses identically. This is a finite registered region, not a q-centred image neighborhood or a dense whole-part certificate.",
    "continuous_first_hit": {
      "direction": "Normalized eye-to-witness ray; reference_distance is Euclidean eye-to-witness distance. No nearest pixel lookup.",
      "triangle_hit_eligibility": "abs(det)>1e-14; barycentric u>=-1e-12, v>=-1e-12, u+v<=1+1e-12; t>1e-10.",
      "first_hit_tie": "Nearest positive t; all hits within 64*float64eps*max(1,abs(nearest)) are co-nearest. Multiple distinct owner IDs produce U (DIFFERENT_PART_DEPTH_TIE); no hit produces U (RAY_MISS).",
      "sample_state": "Using tol=1e-8*max(1,reference_distance): D iff abs(hit_distance-reference_distance)<=tol and owner==designated primary part. A hit strictly in front (difference<-tol) is E iff owner999, otherwise S, including a front surface of the same primary part. Remaining hits are U."
    },
    "active_subset": "Always endpoint0. For axis a, include its3 edge samples when any other face axis is front-facing; include9 samples of face a when that face is front-facing. Front criterion diag(SIGNS[canonical])@(eye-anchor)>1e-12. At least2 front axes are required for target-alone D.",
    "target_alone_and_scene_state_precedence": [
      "geometric_S iff all37 target-alone sample states are S; then target-alone region S.",
      "Otherwise target-alone D iff at least2 front axes and all active target-alone samples D; else target-alone U.",
      "If ANY of all37 projected points is outside closed [0,size-1] in either coordinate, final state U.",
      "Else target-alone S remains S, even if foreign is added; target-alone non-D remains U.",
      "Else all active combined samples E => final E; all active combined samples D => final D; all other mixtures/ties/misses/partial cases => U."
    ],
    "owner_vs_appearance": "Target owners are constructive part IDs; foreign opaque12-triangle cuboid uses ID999 in both ray scene and raster. SAME_TARGET_MATERIAL repeats the same material_rgb recipe/seed after translation compensation, but never merges owner identity. Background has owner<0 in raster; a continuous ray miss is U, not a background semantic label.",
    "raster_semantics": "Independent target-part nearest camera-Z layers, then combine foreign layer999. Integer pixel centres and top-left triangle edge rule; near clipping. Final best depth is fixed first; eligibility is within64 float64ULPs scaled by max(1,abs(best)). Distinct eligible owners set ambiguity and tie_count; lowest numeric owner is stored deterministically but must not be treated as unambiguous. Same-part face ties do not imply ownership U. camera_depth is camera-Z, not continuous ray Euclidean t.",
    "nearest_and_query_diagnostic": "nearest_pixels=floor(xy+.5); valid only finite rounded indices in [0,size). V129 saves nearest-owner/depth/ambiguity separately from continuous witness ray results, and explicitly retains semantic teacher without pixel relabeling. Crop diagnostic U if OOB or ambiguous, else owner<0 BACKGROUND / owner999 FOREIGN / other owner TARGET. These categories never determine original D/E/S."
  },
  "mapping": {
    "V129_primary": "Canonical signs order [---,+--,++-,-+-,--+,+-+,+++, -++] in X-right/Y-down/Z-far. A quarter rotation is [[0,0,1],[0,1,0],[-1,0,0]]^k. Expected literal rotated-sign anchors define permCF_to_canonical by exact equality, with X/Z half extents swapped for odd k. Camera eye is A.T@eye_CF; mesh is not rotated again. Project canonical anchors, then index by perm exactly once. records_CF retain the canonical record/state and rename only the CF role.",
    "boundary": "V132 correspondence_boundary=(CF_slot_to_canonical != historical V4_slot_to_canonical) for the whole base. Historical sensitivity first changes canonical coordinates to [X,Z,-Y], then invokes pinned compute_perm_v4. This is a convention correspondence discrepancy, not pixel boundary/depth tie/query OOB/physical surface ambiguity. All3 fixed bases are boundary true; primary remains declared CF, V4 sensitivity only, no error-minimizing permutation.",
    "V140_distinction": "V140 project_named_virtual_references_once.py concerns separate reconstructed Pallox source, not these V129 scenes. It imports pinned V74 fixed signs/faces/names/outward_normals/normal_facing_permutation by AST, uses provisional source-static world=(Xobj-Cx,Zobj-Cz,-(Yobj-Cy)), projects supplied T, and keeps all8 coordinates. Front cosine margin and projected left/right separation<=1e-10 flag provisional tie ambiguity; semantic states remain U. Virtual-reference mesh distance is diagnostic, never snapping or visibility. V140 cannot certify V129 q association, exact physical corner pixels, or an alternative V129 permutation. The V74 function body was not opened in this review."
  },
